From 2146d2c97bb611aad8a4b538f49312c2e738589a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: amtellezfernandez <177202985+amtellezfernandez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:21:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] runtime: select route plugins through
 route_generator_type

Drop the RouteGeneratorType enum and the parallel route_generator_plugin
field. route_generator_type is now a string: MAP, RECORDED and NONE keep
their built-in meaning, and any other name resolves to an
alpasim.route_generators entry point.

The enum rejected an unknown value when the config was parsed. To keep
that, parse_simulator_config resolves a plugin name at startup, so a typo
fails before services start rather than once per rollout. Built-in
routing still does not import alpasim_plugins; an unknown name without it
installed raises a ValueError instead of an ImportError.
